From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Paslawski <chris@paslawski.me>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 19:45:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] sepolicy: label SurfaceFlinger's virtual-display HWC option

Origin: Local ThinkSmart View port
Source: https://github.com/LineageOS/android_device_mainline_common
License: Apache-2.0 (modified upstream sources)
Base-commit: f49f55117276cc2603fd7f6aeb78b859535f8e8d

SurfaceFlinger reads vendor.display.vds_allow_hwc during initialization,
even when the property is unset. Without a specific context the lookup
attempts to map vendor_default_prop, which SurfaceFlinger cannot read.

Assign this exact boolean to the existing public HWC configuration type
and allow SurfaceFlinger to read that type. Do not grant access to the
default vendor property bucket or change the option's default value.

--- a/sepolicy/vendor/property_contexts
+++ b/sepolicy/vendor/property_contexts
@@ -12,6 +12,7 @@ vendor.dlkm.modules.ready			u:object_r:vendor_dlkm_prop:s0 exact bool
 
 # Graphics (drm_hwc)
 vendor.hwc.drm.device		u:object_r:vendor_hwc_drm_prop:s0 exact string
+vendor.display.vds_allow_hwc	u:object_r:vendor_hwc_drm_prop:s0 exact bool
 
 # Graphics (Mesa)
 vendor.drm.gpu.vendor_name	u:object_r:vendor_mesa_prop:s0
--- a/sepolicy/vendor/surfaceflinger.te
+++ b/sepolicy/vendor/surfaceflinger.te
@@ -1 +1,2 @@
 gpu_access(surfaceflinger)
+get_prop(surfaceflinger, vendor_hwc_drm_prop)
